# What the website image build may see. Without this file the build context is
# the whole working tree, so `COPY . .` carries a developer's node_modules, an
# older build output and whatever file modes that tree happens to have into the
# image. The published files inherit those modes, and a file the NGINX worker
# cannot read is answered with 403 rather than served.
#
# Everything the build needs is a tracked source file, a manifest or the
# lockfile; everything below is produced, local or irrelevant to it.

# Produced by a build, and rebuilt inside the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/dist-ssr
**/dist-deploy
**/dist-consent
**/dist-deploy-consent
**/dist-published
**/dist-deploy-published
**/target
**/.vite
**/.turbo

# History, editor and operating system state.
.git
.github
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store

# Test output, caches and reports.
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/coverage
**/.pnpm-store
**/vendor

# Local configuration. A secret must never reach a build context at all.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
